--- body ---
## Context
Ticket 0084 fixes the crash/dir-creation bug when --help is passed to a
subcommand. This ticket goes further: make --help a first-class, documented
feature — output goes to stdout, the usage header documents the flag, and
any COMMAND --help routes to the global command list.

Per-command detailed help strings (one paragraph per command) are deferred
to ticket 0090, which depends on the doc-comment enrichment in 0089.

## Actions
1. Move `printUsage()` output from stderr to stdout.
2. Document `[--help]` in the global usage header line.
3. `erg COMMAND --help` already routes to `printUsage()` via the 0084 guard.

## Test
```
erg --help          # output on stdout, header contains [--help]
erg init --help     # exits 0, output on stdout (not stderr)
```

## Exit criteria
- [x] `printUsage()` writes to stdout
- [x] Usage header reads `Usage: erg COMMAND [--help] [args...]`
- [x] `erg COMMAND --help` exits 0 and prints to stdout
- [x] `make test` passes
- [ ] Per-command detailed help strings — deferred to ticket 0090
